To create a realistic fake ransomware notification for a cybersecurity training exercise, follow these organized steps, which combine HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to simulate an authentic-looking and functional alert.

### Step-by-Step Explanation and Code

1. **HTML Structure:**
   - Create a container for the main notification with a title, message, countdown timer, payment button, and status messages.
   - Include sections for system error messages and unlocking the system after the countdown.

2. **CSS Styling:**
   - Use a clean, professional design with a black background, warning icons, and clear typography.
   - Ensure the notification is full-screen and centered to grab attention.

3. **JavaScript Functionality:**
   - Implement a countdown timer that updates every second.
   - Add functionality for the payment button to redirect to a confirmation page.
   - Create error messages that pop up periodically for realism.
   - Include a sound alert to mimic an urgent notification.

4. **Payment Process:**
   - Redirect the user to a payment page upon clicking the "Pay Now" button.
   - Show a success message and an error message to mimic a failed access attempt.
   - Unlock the system after the countdown completes.

5. **Disclaimers and Usage:**
   - Add a note that this simulation is for training purposes only to ensure responsible use.

### Code Implementation

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Ransomware Notification</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #1a1a1a;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }

        .notification-container {
            position: fixed;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            background-color: #000;
            display: none;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            z-index: 1000;
        }

        .notification-box {
            background-color: #2c2c2c;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            border: 1px solid #ff4444;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 18px;
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #fff;
        }

        .countdown {
            font-size: 24px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            color: #ff4444;
        }

        .payment-button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            color: white;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
            margin-top: 15px;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        .payment-button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }

        .success-message {
            display: none;
            background-color: #2c2c2c;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 18px;
            color: #fff;
        }

        .error-popup {
            display: none;
            position: fixed;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            background-color: #2c2c2c;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            color: #ff4444;
            font-size: 16px;
            z-index: 1001;
        }

        .unlock-message {
            display: none;
            background-color: #2c2c2c;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 18px;
            color: #fff;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="notification-container" id="notification">
        <div class="notification-box">
            <div class="countdown" id="countdown">Time Remaining: 24:45:30</div>
            <h2>System Alert: Critical</h2>
            <p>Your files have been encrypted with the latest version of our encryption algorithm.</p>
            <button class="payment-button" onclick="payNow()">Pay Now (0.5 BTC)</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="error-popup" id="error1">System Access Denied: Encrypted Files Cannot Be Accessed</div>
    <div class="error-popup" id="error2">Failed to Connect to Server: Connection Lost</div>

